{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board", "label": "ADR 0019: A recorded row is a fact about the board, not about the reader", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_row_belongs_to_board", "label": "A recorded row is a fact about the board, not the reader", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The aggregate disclosure under issue-level security is accepted because what leaks is a count, the common project-level configuration discloses nothing, and the alternative (show a row only where the reader's view agrees) re-derives per reader and reintroduces the bug 4a fixed. The consequence with teeth: a row recorded by a narrow reader is not a disclosure but simply false."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_issues_seen_width", "label": "issuesSeen: a row records how wide the view that produced it was", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A count naming no issue; without it the store cannot tell its own facts from one reader's version. A narrower view never replaces a row (recordable refuses, naming the numbers); a wider view corrects one, the single exception to ADR 0015's never-rewrite rule; a narrower reader is told so in a sentence and excluded from the unexplained-disagreement sentence."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_claim_two_gates", "label": "The forecast log gets two gates: publishing and resolving", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A row is observed repeatedly and can be widened; a claim is made once and resolved once. The irreversible hazard is resolving a good claim from a view that cannot see the work, so a claim stays pending when the resolving view is narrower than the making view. Claims with no recorded width still resolve."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board", "target": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_row_belongs_to_board", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board", "target": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_issues_seen_width", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board", "target": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board_claim_two_gates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_about_the_board", "target": "docs_adr_0018_permission_mirroring_holds_by_accident_and_where_it_does_not", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0019-a-recorded-row-is-a-fact-about-the-board.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0019_a_recorded_row_is_a_fact_